examples/service/skeid.yaml declares:

  admin:
    api_key_env: SKEID_ADMIN_API_KEY

but reload_config only understands admin_api_key or admin.api_key. In config-managed mode an
absent key sets admin_api_key to the empty string, which disables /skeid/* entirely (404).
So the shipped stack sets SKEID_ADMIN_API_KEY in compose and the admin API is dead anyway.

Fix: support api_key_env in reload_config, consistent with the existing password_env idiom in
usage_store. Test: config with api_key_env + env set => /skeid/nodes answers 401 without a
token and 200 with it.
Fixed: reload_config now supports admin_api_key_env and admin.api_key_env, consistent with usage_store password_env. Regression test in t/21-admin-auth.t.
